      "reading_order": 0,
      "text": "2D RELATIVE SPATIAL POSITION ATTENTION IN MULTI-COLUMN DOCUMENT TRANSFORMERS",
      "is_critical": true,
      "critical_category": "document_header"
    },
    {
      "id": "elem-402",
      "type": "text",
      "bbox": { "x": 50.0, "y": 120.0, "width": 460.0, "height": 95.0 },
      "reading_order": 1,
      "text": "Column 1 Architecture: In contrast to 1D sequence models that linearize text tokens, multi-column document transformers incorporate continuous 2D coordinate projections to preserve structural layout geometry across horizontal column boundaries.",
      "is_critical": false,
      "metadata": { "column": 0 }
    },
    {
      "id": "elem-404",
      "type": "text",
      "bbox": { "x": 50.0, "y": 230.0, "width": 460.0, "height": 85.0 },
      "reading_order": 2,
      "text": "Spatial Attention Bias Formulation: Given bounding box centroids (x_i, y_i) and (x_j, y_j), the relative spatial bias between token i and token j is computed across orthogonal spatial projections:",
      "is_critical": false,
      "metadata": { "column": 0 }
    },
    {
      "id": "elem-405",
      "type": "formula",
      "bbox": { "x": 50.0, "y": 330.0, "width": 460.0, "height": 65.0 },
      "reading_order": 3,
      "text": "Bias(i, j) = b_x(x_i - x_j) + b_y(y_i - y_j)",
      "is_critical": true,
      "critical_category": "primary_theorem",
      "metadata": { "subgroup": "rare_case" },
      "formula": {
        "latex": "\\text{Bias}(i, j) = \\mathbf{b}_{x}(x_i - x_j) + \\mathbf{b}_{y}(y_i - y_j)",
        "text": "Bias(i, j) = b_x(x_i - x_j) + b_y(y_i - y_j)",
        "formula_type": "display"
      }
    },
